Description: Declarative management of one appliance instance
 Keel describes one appliance instance in a single file and applies it
 idempotently. It is compatible with TurnKey Linux appliances: the spec is
 rendered into the inithooks conf variables the existing firstboot hooks
 already read, so no hook has to know that the spec exists.
 .
 The library is the only implementation. The keel command and confconsole
 are both clients of it, so every operation runs headless from the same
 code path.
